Go++ third-party notices
========================

The Go++ front end contains code and tests derived from the Go project.

Files
-----
- compiler/lib/Lex/Lexer.cpp
    ported from go/scanner (scanner.go)
- compiler/lib/Parse/Parser.cpp
    ported from go/parser (parser.go)
- compiler/include/gopp/Basic/DiagnosticIDs.def
    the lexer and parser messages of go/scanner and go/parser
- compiler/lib/Basic/UnicodeTables.inc (generated by tools/gen-unicode)
    derived from the tables of Go's unicode package
- tests/unit/Lex/GoScannerPortTest.cpp
    ported from go/scanner (scanner_test.go)
- tests/unit/Parse/GoParserPortTest.cpp
    ported from go/parser (short_test.go and testdata)
- compiler/lib/Format/Printer.cpp
    ported from go/printer (printer.go, nodes.go)
- compiler/lib/Format/TabWriter.cpp, TabWriter.h
    ported from text/tabwriter (tabwriter.go)
- compiler/lib/Format/Format.cpp (import sorting)
    ported from go/ast (import.go, SortImports)
- tests/fmt/Inputs/goprinter/*.input
    copied from go/printer/testdata
- tests/fmt/Inputs/gofmt/*.input
    copied from cmd/gofmt/testdata
- tests/fuzz/corpus/goprinter-*.go, tests/fuzz/corpus/gofmt-*.go
    copied from go/printer/testdata and cmd/gofmt/testdata (fuzz seeds)
- compiler/lib/Sema/*.cpp, compiler/lib/Sema/Checker.h,
  compiler/include/gopp/Sema/*.h
    the checker is ported from cmd/compile/internal/types2 and the constants
    follow go/constant; the files say which parts
- tests/sema/conformance/testdata/{check,fixedbugs,spec,examples}/*.go
    copied from internal/types/testdata (the types2 conformance suite)
- tests/unit/Sema/ConstantTest.cpp
    ported from go/constant (value_test.go)

